i am so happy do you want to know why  because jehovah god  has given me the bible in asl  which is sign language to help me  understand  a 15-year labor of love jehovah's  witnesses released the first american  sign language bible to the deaf  community  in early 2020 a translation milestone  inspiring organizations  and the local community for us it's been  a 15-year journey  and we can finally say uh it's complete  it's so exhilarating to be able to have  the entire bible  in asl i enjoy being able to watch it  to research it's it's all ready for me  there when it wasn't translated into  american sign language i had to wait  so long and i waited patiently until it  was completed  almost 900 000 complete bibles  have been downloaded uh 2.4 million  complete bible books have been  downloaded and 41 million  individual chapters of this asl  translation have been downloaded  so it's affected many many more than  just jehovah's witnesses because in this  country  those who speak asl those who use asl  only amount to about 10 000 in  congregations of jehovah's witnesses  and only about 2500 of them are actual  deaf from the deaf community the rest  are those who support them in their  congregations  sign language translation is unique the  visual language requires translation  from text to video  his image of what the bible is trying to  say to us  should be the same as a person reading  the bowl in english or any other  language  as a sign language interpreter here in  nevada i work very hard to try and give  an accurate interpretation  but interpreting is kind of like art  you're doing it without  having information beforehand versus the  effort that goes into a translation like  the new world translation  the bible provided for the deaf  could not have come at a better time the  asl bible team were the first to use a  live review panel to ensure a high  quality product that was easy to be  understood by the viewer  so when they when they did a translation  of a text  that was so literal that would it could  only be understood literally  it was often very illogical and it often  meant that the sign language translation  team had to go back to the drawing board  and come up with a revised text that  would be more understandable  our translation system is more thought  for thought rather than  word for word so the concept they're  making sure there's no  missing context concepts or added  concepts  but if that thought can be conveyed in  an accurate way in a meaningful way  that's what it's all about  members in a local sign language  congregation here in las vegas shared  their thoughts on how they felt after  viewing the american sign language bible  for the first time  as a child of two deaf adults i identify  linguistically and culturally with the  deaf community  what i choose to do for my secular work  is i'm an american sign language  interpreter  but as one of jehovah's witnesses i  choose to use the bulk of my time  focusing on a career in teaching the  bible over the years that has been very  difficult  at times because having access to the  bible  in written form doesn't reach their  hearts in the same way as watching it  especially in the last few months well  the last year really because of the  pandemic the isolation is more severe  for members of the deaf community and so  their mental health their emotional  health  has been impacted and so having access  to these  bible scriptures which bring comfort is  is a huge  joy to see hello  my name is richard my name is sign like  this  i am eight years old and i am deaf as  the father of a deaf son  and as immigrants when we moved here  to the united states it was very  difficult in 2019  we moved here to the city of las vegas  and received  great support so we decided to move to  an american sign language congregation  so we could help our son  the very fact that this is the first  bible it's available  freely to anyone who wants to use it  even if they don't agree with what we  say about the teachings of the bible  at least they've got god's word  amazingly the translation work was  carried out by nearly 100 volunteers  the new bible has had a huge impact in  my family in so many ways  in our relationship as a family in me as  a wife  and as a mother now when we all three  sit down to study  the bible we can understand the  questions our son  asks us and i feel a direct connection  with my son  when it comes to reading the bible  watching it in asl i have it downloaded  in an  app on my phone and tablet so i can use  it for study it's  it's all there for me i can use it for  everything that i need  and i love having it there it's just  ready to go  the complete bible in american sign  language or asl is available  for viewing free of charge on their  official website jw.org  and this is really the goal the goal of  jehovah's witnesses  is to get out the gospel the good news  especially  the bible in the language of people's  hearts  reporting from the eight news now  digital news desk i'm your life producer  rocky nash for the full story visit  eightnewsnow.com
 

